steps.message:
The issue was that `Dataset.wrl.georef.georeference()` in `wradlib/georef/polar.py` was incorrectly assigning the units of the x-coordinate (which could be degrees in geographic CRS) to the z-coordinate (height) and the ground range coordinate, both of which are always in meters.

I have modified `wradlib/georef/polar.py` to explicitly set the units for `z_attrs` and `gr_attrs` to `"meters"`.

Verified the fix with the provided MCVE code sample.

```python
# Before fix:
# z_attrs = {"standard_name": "height_above_ground", "units": unit}
# gr_attrs = {"standard_name": "distance_from_radar", "units": unit}

# After fix:
# z_attrs = {"standard_name": "height_above_ground", "units": "meters"}
# gr_attrs = {"standard_name": "distance_from_radar", "units": "meters"}
```

